## Everyday tips

- wear your splint every night
- take short breaks from typing, phone use and gripping tasks
- keep your hands warm, as cold can make symptoms worse
- use a keyboard and mouse that keep your wrist straight

## Gadgets that can help

- jar and bottle openers
- kitchen tools with thick, easy grip handles
- a kettle tipper
- voice typing on your phone or computer

## Look after related conditions

If you have diabetes or an underactive thyroid, keeping them well controlled can help. Losing weight, if you need to, may reduce pressure on the nerve.

## Support

**Versus Arthritis** has information and a free helpline.
